% Power Mobility Devices: LCD L33789 and its Policy Article A52498 (DME
% MACs), read with NCD 280.3 (mobility assistive equipment) and 42 CFR
% 410.38. A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le and
% states when a claim for a power operated vehicle (a scooter, K0800–K0802)
% or a power wheelchair (K0813–K0864, K0890, K0891) or a power assist system
% (E0986) is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY: the basic criteria A–C every device
% needs, the scooter criteria D–I, the power wheelchair criteria (no scooter
% would do; J or K; L–O), the weight class of the device, and the added
% criteria of single and multiple power option chairs, Group 3, Group 5 and
% power assist. Group 2 scooters and Group 4 chairs are never covered (the
% LCD: "added capabilities that are not needed for use in the home"), nor a
% device the PDAC has not coded (K0899): no rule concludes them.
%
% How the criteria are read. The LCD's criteria are clinical findings about
% the beneficiary — a significant mobility limitation, that walking aids
% would not resolve it, that the beneficiary cannot self-propel a manual
% wheelchair, cannot use a scooter, can operate the chair, will use it at
% home... — made by the treating practitioner in the face-to-face encounter
% and accepted or rejected on review: each is the judged template of
% dmepos.le, "the finding F about B is established" (or unsupported), with
% who found it and why. Where the LCD offers alternatives (J or K: the
% beneficiary can operate the chair, or a caregiver can; II.1 or II.2: an
% alternative drive control, or a power seating system; III.1 or III.2: a
% tilt and recline system, or a ventilator on the chair; D, E or F failing
% for a scooter) they are ONE finding with the alternatives as its reasons,
% so that a recorded finding closes the question. The findings this policy
% reads, and the criterion each stands for:
%   significant mobility limitation (A); walking aids insufficient (B);
%   manual wheelchair not self propellable (C); able to transfer to scooter
%   safely (D); capabilities sufficient for scooter (E); home accommodates
%   scooter (F); scooter will significantly improve daily activities (H);
%   willing to use scooter at home (I); scooter ruled out (a power wheelchair:
%   D, E or F fails); power wheelchair can be safely operated (J or K); home
%   accommodates power wheelchair (M); power wheelchair will significantly
%   improve daily activities (N); willing to use power wheelchair at home (O);
%   single power option justified (II.1 or II.2); multiple power option
%   justified (III.1 or III.2); qualifying group 3 diagnosis (IV.B); expected
%   to grow in height (Group 5). What the record states as fact — the
% beneficiary's weight, the specialty evaluation, the ATP's involvement, a
% ventilator on the chair, the duration of need — is a scenario fact. The
% device's group, weight class and power options come from its HCPCS code
% (facts citing the CMS code list).
%
% The payment conditions the policy adds (Policy Article A52498, LCD
% "Documentation requirements"): the practitioner who examined the beneficiary
% writes the order; the supplier assesses the home on or before delivery;
% delivery within six months of an affirmed prior authorization.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    the condition of *a beneficiary* is reversible with a length of need under three months; undefined.
    the order for *an item* was written by the practitioner who conducted the face-to-face encounter; undefined.
    the supplier performed an on-site evaluation of the home for *an item*; undefined.
    % the codes
    PMD code *a code* describes *a kind* of group *a number* in weight class *a class* with *an option*.
    the weight range of class *a class* is *a number* to *an other number* pounds.
    % derived
    *a beneficiary* meets the basic PMD coverage criteria.
    *a beneficiary* meets the scooter criteria.
    *a beneficiary* cannot use a scooter.
    *a beneficiary* meets the power wheelchair criteria.
    *an item* can be safely operated for *a beneficiary*.
    the weight of *a beneficiary* fits the class of *an item*.
    *an item* is needed for at least three months.
    *an item* was selected with a specialty evaluation and an assistive technology professional.
    *a beneficiary* meets the single power option criteria.
    *a beneficiary* meets the multiple power option criteria.
    *a beneficiary* meets the group 3 criteria.
    the delivery of *an item* is within six months of its prior authorization.

the knowledge base pmd includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base pmd includes:

LCD L33789 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33789".
the text of LCD L33789 is at "sources/lcd/L33789.txt".
Policy Article A52498 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52498".
the text of Policy Article A52498 is at "sources/article/A52498.txt".
NCD 280 3 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/ncd.aspx?ncdid=219".
the text of NCD 280 3 is at "sources/ncd/NCD_280.3.txt".

