PMD code "K0891" describes power wheelchair of group 5 in weight class standard with multiple power option, as stated in LCD L33789, confer "A Group 5 (Pediatric) PWC with Single Power Option (K0890) or with Multiple Power Options (K0891) is covered if".

% The weight each class is covered for: at most the capacity, at least 95
% percent of the next lower class's.
the weight range of class standard is 0 to 300 pounds,
    as stated in LCD L33789, confer "The beneficiary’s weight is less than or equal to the weight capacity of the power wheelchair that is provided and greater than or equal to 95% of the weight capacity of the next lower weight class PWC".
the weight range of class heavy duty is 285 to 450 pounds,
    as stated in LCD L33789, confer "a Heavy Duty PWC is covered for a beneficiary weighing 285 – 450 pounds".
the weight range of class very heavy duty is 428 to 600 pounds,
    as stated in LCD L33789, confer "a Very Heavy Duty PWC is covered for a beneficiary weighing 428 – 600 pounds".
the weight range of class extra heavy duty is 570 to 10000 pounds,
    as stated in LCD L33789, confer "an Extra Heavy Duty PWC is covered for a beneficiary weighing 570 pounds or more".

section applicability is:

rule pmd_codes with provenance Policy Article A52498,
        confer "Power mobility devices are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the policy for code a code is pmd
    if PMD code the code describes a kind of group a number in weight class a class with an option.

the policy for code "E0986" is pmd,
    as stated in LCD L33789, confer "A power assist system (E0986) for a manual wheelchair is covered if all of the following criteria are met".

rule pmd_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52498,
        confer "Power mobility devices are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is pmd.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Scooters (Group 1 POVs): the basic criteria A–C and D–I.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule pmd_scooter with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "A POV is covered if all of the basic coverage criteria (A-C) have been met and if criteria D-I are also met":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and PMD code the code describes scooter of group 1 in weight class a class with an option
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the basic PMD coverage criteria
    and the beneficiary meets the scooter criteria
    and the weight of the beneficiary fits the class of the item
    and the item is needed for at least three months.

% Criteria A, B and C: the findings of the face-to-face encounter.
rule pmd_basic with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "All of the following basic criteria (A-C) must be met for a power mobility device":
a beneficiary meets the basic PMD coverage criteria
    if the finding significant mobility limitation about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding walking aids insufficient about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding manual wheelchair not self propellable about the beneficiary is established.

rule pmd_scooter_criteria with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "The beneficiary is able to: Safely transfer to and from a POV, and Operate the tiller steering system, and Maintain postural stability and position while operating the POV in the home":
a beneficiary meets the scooter criteria
    if the finding able to transfer to scooter safely about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding capabilities sufficient for scooter about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding home accommodates scooter about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding scooter will significantly improve daily activities about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding willing to use scooter at home about the beneficiary is established.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Power wheelchairs: the basic criteria, no scooter would do, J or K, L–O,
% and the added criteria of each group.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule pmd_pwc_group_1_2 with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "A Group 1 PWC (K0813, K0814, K0815, K0816) or a Group 2 PWC (K0820, K0821, K0822, K0823, K0824, K0825, K0826, K0827, K0828, K0829) is covered if all of the coverage criteria (a)-(e) for a PWC are met and the wheelchair is appropriate for the beneficiary’s weight":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and PMD code the code describes power wheelchair of group a number in weight class a class with no power option
    and the number <= 2
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the basic PMD coverage criteria
    and the beneficiary cannot use a scooter
    and the beneficiary meets the power wheelchair criteria
    and the item can be safely operated for the beneficiary
    and the weight of the beneficiary fits the class of the item
    and the item is needed for at least three months.

rule pmd_pwc_group_2_single with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "A Group 2 Single Power Option PWC (K0835, K0836, K0837, K0838, K0839, K0840) is covered if all of the coverage criteria (a)-(e) for a PWC are met and if":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and PMD code the code describes power wheelchair of group 2 in weight class a class with single power option
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the basic PMD coverage criteria
    and the beneficiary cannot use a scooter
    and the beneficiary meets the power wheelchair criteria
    and the item can be safely operated for the beneficiary
    and the weight of the beneficiary fits the class of the item
    and the item is needed for at least three months
    and the beneficiary meets the single power option criteria
    and the item was selected with a specialty evaluation and an assistive technology professional.

rule pmd_pwc_group_2_multiple with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "A Group 2 Multiple Power Option PWC (K0841, K0842, K0843) is covered if all of the coverage criteria (a)-(e) for a PWC are met and if":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and PMD code the code describes power wheelchair of group 2 in weight class a class with multiple power option
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the basic PMD coverage criteria
    and the beneficiary cannot use a scooter
    and the beneficiary meets the power wheelchair criteria
    and the item can be safely operated for the beneficiary
    and the weight of the beneficiary fits the class of the item
    and the item is needed for at least three months
    and the beneficiary meets the multiple power option criteria
    and the item was selected with a specialty evaluation and an assistive technology professional.

rule pmd_pwc_group_3 with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "A Group 3 PWC with no power options (K0848, K0849, K0850, K0851, K0852, K0853, K0854, K0855) is covered if":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and PMD code the code describes power wheelchair of group 3 in weight class a class with no power option
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the basic PMD coverage criteria
    and the beneficiary cannot use a scooter
    and the beneficiary meets the power wheelchair criteria
    and the item can be safely operated for the beneficiary
