    and the item was selected with a specialty evaluation and an assistive technology professional.

rule pmd_power_assist with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "The beneficiary has been self-propelling in a manual wheelchair for at least one year":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "E0986"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the basic PMD coverage criteria
    and the beneficiary has been self propelling a manual wheelchair for at least one year
    and the item was selected with a specialty evaluation and an assistive technology professional.

% A power wheelchair needs what a scooter cannot give: the beneficiary fails
% one of the scooter criteria D, E or F.
rule pmd_no_scooter with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "The beneficiary does not meet coverage criterion D, E, or F for a POV":
a beneficiary cannot use a scooter
    if the finding scooter ruled out about the beneficiary is established.

% Criteria J and K.
rule pmd_criteria_j_k with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "The beneficiary has the mental and physical capabilities to safely operate the power wheelchair that is provided":
an item can be safely operated for a beneficiary
    if the finding power wheelchair can be safely operated about the beneficiary is established.

% Criteria M, N and O.
rule pmd_pwc_criteria with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "The beneficiary’s home provides adequate access between rooms, maneuvering space, and surfaces for the operation of the power wheelchair that is provided":
a beneficiary meets the power wheelchair criteria
    if the finding home accommodates power wheelchair about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding power wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding willing to use power wheelchair at home about the beneficiary is established.

% Criteria G and L: the weight class.
rule pmd_weight with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "The beneficiary’s weight is less than or equal to the weight capacity of the power wheelchair that is provided and greater than or equal to 95% of the weight capacity of the next lower weight class PWC":
the weight of a beneficiary fits the class of an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and PMD code the code describes a kind of group a number in weight class a class with an option
    and the weight range of class the class is a low to a high pounds
    and the weight of the beneficiary is a weight pounds
    and the weight >= the low
    and the weight <= the high.

% A reversible condition with a short need is denied.
rule pmd_duration with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "A power mobility device will be denied as not reasonable and necessary if the underlying condition is reversible and the length of need is less than 3 months":
an item is needed for at least three months
    if the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the condition of the beneficiary is reversible with a length of need under three months.

% The single and multiple power option criteria (II and III).
rule pmd_single_power with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "The beneficiary requires a drive control interface other than a hand or chin-operated standard proportional joystick":
a beneficiary meets the single power option criteria
    if the finding single power option justified about the beneficiary is established.

rule pmd_multiple_power with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "The beneficiary meets coverage criteria for a power tilt and recline seating system":
a beneficiary meets the multiple power option criteria
    if the finding multiple power option justified about the beneficiary is established.

rule pmd_group_3 with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "The beneficiary's mobility limitation is due to a neurological condition, myopathy, or congenital skeletal deformity":
a beneficiary meets the group 3 criteria
    if the finding qualifying group 3 diagnosis about the beneficiary is established.

rule pmd_specialty with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "The beneficiary has had a specialty evaluation that was performed by a licensed/certified medical professional, such as a physical therapist (PT) or occupational therapist (OT), or practitioner who has specific training and experience in rehabilitation wheelchair evaluations":
an item was selected with a specialty evaluation and an assistive technology professional
    if the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary had a specialty evaluation by a licensed medical professional with no financial relationship with the supplier for the item
    and a RESNA certified assistive technology professional employed by the supplier was directly involved in the selection of the item.

section remedy is:

% The policy's own conditions of payment.
rule pmd_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52498,
        confer "payment may not be made for a motorized or power wheelchair unless the treating practitioner conducts the face-to-face encounter and writes the Standard Written Order (SWO)":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is pmd
    and the claim is for an item
    and the order for the item was written by the practitioner who conducted the face-to-face encounter
    and the supplier performed an on-site evaluation of the home for the item
    and the delivery of the item is within six months of its prior authorization.

rule pmd_pa_delivery with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "For PWCs that go through Advance Determination of Medicare Coverage (ADMC) or Prior Authorization (PA) and receive an affirmative determination, the delivery must be within 6 months following the determination":
the delivery of an item is within six months of its prior authorization
    if prior authorization for the item was affirmed on a date
    and the item was delivered on an other date
    and the other date is a number days after the date
    and the number >= 0
    and the number <= 183.

rule pmd_no_pa with provenance LCD L33789,
        confer "For PWCs that go through Advance Determination of Medicare Coverage (ADMC) or Prior Authorization (PA) and receive an affirmative determination, the delivery must be within 6 months following the determination":
the delivery of an item is within six months of its prior authorization
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the code is on the required prior authorization list.
